WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
ZRPF connects application execution, proof tasks, leaf proofs, recursive roots, and governed admission.

00:07.000 --> 00:15.000
Current local evidence contains four Spot compatibility leaves, two level-one structural receipts, and one level-two structural root.

00:15.000 --> 00:22.000
Leaves and aggregates share the NodeJournalV3 interface: scope, counts, identities, commitments, and child roots.

00:22.000 --> 00:29.000
Proof integrity and data availability are separate obligations. A data root alone does not prove that data can be retrieved.

00:29.000 --> 00:36.000
The prover supplies bytes. Guests, hosts, and governed policy decide whether those bytes authorize a claim.

00:36.000 --> 00:43.000
Proposed admission commits application state, replay protection, carry state, availability evidence, and rewards atomically.

00:43.000 --> 00:48.000
Current evidence, proposed architecture, and benchmark targets must remain visibly distinct.
